Since `inspect.isroutine(p)` is `False`, it skips the first block.
Since `inspect.isclass(p)` is `False`, it skips the second block.
Then it checks `iscoroutinefunction(p.__call__)`, which is `False`.

So it returns `False`.

But if we just called `iscoroutinefunction(p)`, it would return `True`!

So the fix for `partial(async_func)` is indeed to remove the `inspect.isroutine` check or change it.

